{
  "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
  "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Settled law recognizes the scientific, legal, and moral truth that most children, even those who commit grievous crimes, are capable of redemption. After Miller and Montgomery, there is no denying that the permanent incorrigibility rule is settled law. Only juvenile homicide offenders who are permanently incorrigible may be sentenced to life without parole."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court should enforce settled law by remanding for an answer to the decisive question: Is Brett Jones, who committed a crime just weeks after turning 15, permanently incorrigible?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm having just a little trouble figuring out what exactly it is that you're looking for. We know it can't be a formal finding, as I think you indicated, because of Miller and Montgomery's statements. And, obviously, you want more than just a hearing at which you'd have an opportunity to raise the --the arguments. But what is it in the middle there? Is it just a statement on the record at some point during -- during a hearing? Is it, I don't know, some kind of informal hearing -- finding? What exactly do you -- do you need?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, in your cert petition and in your briefing, you frame the question presented as a narrow one about the need for an express finding of permanent incorrigibility."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Shapiro, what -- what you just said is exactly what I want to ask you about, because your argument is that Miller and Montgomery set out not just a process, not just a rule that you'd have to be considered, but, instead, a rule -- a rule -- a substantive rule that you can give an LWOP sentence only to a small category of people, call them the irredeemables or the incorrigibles or what have you."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Good morning, Mr. Shapiro. I have a question about an as-applied Eighth Amendment challenge here. I -- I take it that you think that Mr. Jones can bring such a challenge?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0001-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And to allow the permanent incorrigibility rule to be flouted is to discard Miller and Montgomery and to undermine stare decisis and the interest in stability that it protects."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Nobile",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. NOBILE: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: In 2013, Jones's mandatory life-without-parole sentence for the brutal murder of his grandfather was set aside after the Mississippi Supreme Court held that Miller versus Alabama announced a substantive rule of constitutional law prior to this Court holding the same in Montgomery versus Louisiana. Miller held that mandatory juvenile life-without-parole sentences are unconstitutional because they pose too great a risk of disproportionate punishment. The constitutional flaw in such mandatory schemes is that they make youth and all that accompanies it irrelevant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0001-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF KRISSY C. NOBILE ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the -- the primary disagreement that we have with Petitioner Jones's argument is he continuously relates this to Atkins and Ford, that permanent incorrigibility really in abstract is an objective type of a fact."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the substantive right at issue in Miller is the protection against grossly disproportionate punishment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does Miller, after Montgomery, say that in order to sentence a juvenile to life without parole, he must be incorrigible, all right, permanently incorrigible?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And if I could just interrupt you there, Ms. Nobile, do you mean to say that it satisfies Teague if there is a process rule that has an effect on substantive outcomes?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think you proceed. I think you look at the process that Miller itself prescribed because that process is going to effectuate a substantive rule."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And what would the standard be? Not permanent incorrigibility, I take it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Nobile",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it a more broad question of was this grossly disproportionate?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Frederick Liu",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0003-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Miller does not require trial courts to make an affirmative finding of permanent incorrigibility."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose a judge says this after a sentencing hearing: I -- I don't think this minor who committed this crime a month short of his 18th birthday is transiently immature. I think this person is highly intelligent and very mature. But I can't say that after 25 years in prison he can't be rehabilitated, if he's released after 25 years, he will commit other crimes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 79,
        "start": 79
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think Ms. Nobile talked about an \"all things considered\" way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Frederick Liu",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0003-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 79,
        "start": 79
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I think it's a pretty well-accepted form of procedural error that when a court says contradictory things, we send it back for the court to clear things up."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David M. Shapiro",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I want to be very clear that we are not -- we are not asking for any sort of formal or affirmative or express or magic words type of finding requirement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Friend from Mississippi",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0004-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My friend from Mississippi said that a weakness of our position is that we haven't laid out all of the details."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0004-0001",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But what there must absolutely be is a determination, implicit or explicit, that the defendant is incapable of rehabilitation before he or she is sentenced to life without parole."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-18-1259",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ca0e5a025f6185bceb8c1932f041682045fb08ec0a6e3567da54f794b7d9b643",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ca0e5a025f61-0004-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:27 a.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
